--- Dowker-Kent-type sets: global projectors onto the evolving state itself ---
  trial 0: max |D| = 2.57e-16  (P1 = projector onto a random-tilted global vector; P2 = its evolved image) -> exactly consistent, no TPS, no record structure
  trial 1: max |D| = 2.60e-16  (P1 = projector onto a random-tilted global vector; P2 = its evolved image) -> exactly consistent, no TPS, no record structure
  trial 2: max |D| = 3.15e-16  (P1 = projector onto a random-tilted global vector; P2 = its evolved image) -> exactly consistent, no TPS, no record structure
  => consistency admits sets built from arbitrary global (non-local, non-record) projectors.
     Selecting the quasi-classical set needs a supplied projector family: local slot (split), a basis class
     (coarse-graining), and the time sequence - all access data.

